※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4473

※ A loop comes to one type, whichever way it was left: the block after it is
※ reached down every one of those ways and reads one thing.  So every `break`
※ in a loop and its `else` arm all give that one type, and nothing is widened
※ to make two of them meet.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let found: u8 = while §counting true:
        break §counting 1u8
    else:
        2u16
    found
